1
00:00:14,140 --> 00:00:17,360
Enyaba, there's something
I'd like to ask you.

2
00:00:17,740 --> 00:00:19,580
What does it mean to live?

3
00:00:20,280 --> 00:00:22,920
It's to obtain all that one desires.

4
00:00:23,400 --> 00:00:27,820
If you were to distill life into its
essence, that is what it would be.

5
00:00:28,500 --> 00:00:33,140
A lust for riches, a desire for
fame, food, love, and lovers.

6
00:00:33,440 --> 00:00:35,040
That is life's goal.

7
00:00:36,300 --> 00:00:39,320
But one must always fight
to get what one wants.

8
00:00:39,560 --> 00:00:41,740
Isn't that correct, Enyaba?

9
00:00:42,880 --> 00:00:43,710
Indeed.

10
00:00:45,380 --> 00:00:49,980
And if the battle is lost and one
fails to obtain what one desires most,

11
00:00:50,160 --> 00:00:51,740
the result is frustration,

12
00:00:52,060 --> 00:00:53,637
pain, and a sense of failure.

13
00:00:53,720 --> 00:00:58,540
One carries the wound into the
future, into the next fearful battle.

14
00:00:59,720 --> 00:01:04,014
I believe conquering that fear once
and for all is what it means to live.

15
00:01:04,600 --> 00:01:09,040
The one who stands at the pinnacle
is the one who has no fear.

16
00:01:10,400 --> 00:01:12,180
Do you understand, Enyaba?

17
00:01:12,900 --> 00:01:17,760
I was the one who told you about the
existence of your stand and how to use it.

18
00:01:17,920 --> 00:01:20,060
Also, you have an immortal body.

19
00:01:20,540 --> 00:01:22,817
Is there anything you could possibly fear?

20
00:01:22,900 --> 00:01:25,380
Perhaps, old woman. Hmm.

21
00:01:25,780 --> 00:01:27,720
What burdens you, my lord?

22
00:01:28,100 --> 00:01:30,140
The Joestar bloodline.

23
00:01:31,420 --> 00:01:32,250
Hmm? Joestar?

24
00:01:32,680 --> 00:01:33,740
They worry you?

25
00:01:33,920 --> 00:01:35,760
Those worms are mere trash.

26
00:01:36,020 --> 00:01:39,340
Your enemies are no match
for your stand. Yes,

27
00:01:39,580 --> 00:01:41,697
but I must believe it's
destiny when the lives of

28
00:01:41,780 --> 00:01:44,377
those worms are so thoroughly
entangled with mine.

29
00:01:44,460 --> 00:01:48,417
It is a fate that has been written
for us all from the very beginning.

30
00:01:48,500 --> 00:01:49,960
Let me be clear.

31
00:01:50,420 --> 00:01:52,920
It is not the Joestars that I fear,

32
00:01:53,100 --> 00:01:56,557
but the fact that I can never
underestimate their bloodline.

33
00:01:56,640 --> 00:01:58,920
In order to obliterate all fear,

34
00:01:59,200 --> 00:02:03,259
I have decided that I must remove
the Joestars from the cogs of fate.

35
00:02:03,920 --> 00:02:06,977
You want to go and eliminate
them yourself simply

36
00:02:07,060 --> 00:02:10,119
because you feel that they
cannot be underestimated?

37
00:02:10,660 --> 00:02:11,490
Yes.

38
00:02:11,900 --> 00:02:12,730
Foolishness!

39
00:02:12,813 --> 00:02:15,117
You should never engage
in such trivial matters.

40
00:02:15,200 --> 00:02:16,937
They are beneath someone of your stature.

41
00:02:17,020 --> 00:02:20,300
I have sent seven stand-users
to command. The Empress,

42
00:02:20,620 --> 00:02:25,157
the Wheel of Fortune, the Hangman, and
Temperance, the Emperor, and the Devil.

43
00:02:25,240 --> 00:02:28,597
All of them on the move and ready
to strike whenever you call.

44
00:02:28,680 --> 00:02:33,340
Thanks to these allies, you need not
take any action yourself, Lord Dio.

45
00:03:01,480 --> 00:03:04,280
Let's go.

46
00:03:32,180 --> 00:03:33,497
Thank

47
00:03:33,580 --> 00:03:34,897
you

48
00:03:34,980 --> 00:03:41,797
so

49
00:03:41,880 --> 00:03:46,940
much for watching.

50
00:04:19,640 --> 00:04:20,640
A freighter!

51
00:04:20,840 --> 00:04:22,193
I didn't see it at all!

52
00:04:24,280 --> 00:04:26,637
Jotaro, something's
bothering you, isn't it?

53
00:04:26,720 --> 00:04:29,657
Are you worried there might be
another stand user on this freighter?

54
00:04:29,740 --> 00:04:32,034
It's not ideal, but we could handle it.

55
00:04:32,520 --> 00:04:33,350
Not quite.

56
00:04:33,433 --> 00:04:34,917
Strange they lowered the stairs.

57
00:04:35,000 --> 00:04:38,647
But there's not a single soul
to be seen around here anywhere.

58
00:04:45,860 --> 00:04:48,272
This ship came all this way to rescue us.

59
00:04:48,380 --> 00:04:50,909
There has to be some
sort of crew on board.

60
00:04:51,140 --> 00:04:53,917
Even if they're all stand
users, I'm getting on this boat.

61
00:04:54,000 --> 00:04:55,706
I'm done drifting in circles.

62
00:05:03,580 --> 00:05:04,840
Take my hand, kid.

63
00:05:05,060 --> 00:05:06,295
I'll help you get up.

64
00:05:14,840 --> 00:05:16,740
Good grief.

65
00:05:40,260 --> 00:05:42,240
Hey, what's with this ship?

66
00:05:42,560 --> 00:05:44,597
There's no captain in the control room?

67
00:05:44,680 --> 00:05:46,617
There's no engineer in the radio room?

68
00:05:46,700 --> 00:05:48,077
There's no one anywhere!

69
00:05:48,160 --> 00:05:49,520
And yet, look at this!

70
00:05:49,680 --> 00:05:53,177
All the gauges and machinery are
working properly, just like normal!

71
00:05:53,260 --> 00:05:56,717
Maybe they're just all in the
bathroom with a bad case of the rugs!

72
00:05:56,800 --> 00:05:57,630
Hey!

73
00:05:57,713 --> 00:05:58,656
Isn't anyone around?

74
00:05:58,860 --> 00:06:00,057
You have to see this!

75
00:06:00,140 --> 00:06:00,970
Come here, quick!

76
00:06:01,053 --> 00:06:01,883
Huh?

77
00:06:04,200 --> 00:06:05,030
An ape!

78
00:06:05,400 --> 00:06:07,282
There's an ape inside that cage!

79
00:06:12,720 --> 00:06:16,517
It's an orangutan who the
hell cares about a friggin ape

80
00:06:16,600 --> 00:06:20,012
let's split up and find whoever's
been feeding this thing?

81
00:06:38,240 --> 00:06:42,780
Well, it doesn't appear
to be broken, but...

82
00:06:49,740 --> 00:06:50,570
Avdol!

83
00:06:50,653 --> 00:06:51,483
That's Sailor!

84
00:06:51,566 --> 00:06:52,396
Watch out!

85
00:06:57,520 --> 00:06:58,640
Oh, good grief.

86
00:06:58,900 --> 00:07:03,018
That isn't any way to greet a lady
you've never met before now, is it?

87
00:07:05,020 --> 00:07:07,196
But no one was touching the controls!

88
00:07:07,820 --> 00:07:11,217
I saw that crane move, even though
there was no one operating it.

89
00:07:11,300 --> 00:07:13,597
I don't believe in
ghosts, but what the hell?

90
00:07:13,680 --> 00:07:14,720
I saw it too!

91
00:07:15,080 --> 00:07:17,256
The crane impaled him all on its own!

92
00:07:18,220 --> 00:07:19,397
Keep your guard up.

93
00:07:19,480 --> 00:07:22,057
There's someone hostile here. Hey!

94
00:07:22,140 --> 00:07:23,377
Don't touch the machinery.

95
00:07:23,460 --> 00:07:24,290
You got that?

96
00:07:24,373 --> 00:07:26,197
If it moves or runs on electricity!

97
00:07:26,280 --> 00:07:27,677
Don't lay a finger on it!

98
00:07:27,760 --> 00:07:30,837
If you want to live, then
you'll do exactly as I tell you!

99
00:07:30,920 --> 00:07:31,750
Understand!

100
00:07:31,833 --> 00:07:35,400
Get into the cabin below and stay
there until I tell you otherwise!

101
00:07:40,520 --> 00:07:43,617
Did any one of you see even a
glimpse of a stand just now?

102
00:07:43,700 --> 00:07:44,757
I didn't.

103
00:07:44,840 --> 00:07:45,737
My apologies.

104
00:07:45,820 --> 00:07:48,697
I was the closest to the
crane and yet I felt nothing.

105
00:07:48,780 --> 00:07:50,457
I should have been able to send something!

106
00:07:50,540 --> 00:07:51,370
All right!

107
00:07:51,453 --> 00:07:54,812
I'll send Hierophant Green to
take a look around the ship!

108
00:08:02,580 --> 00:08:04,757
I have no idea what's going on!

109
00:08:04,840 --> 00:08:06,517
But scary things keep happening!

110
00:08:06,600 --> 00:08:08,306
Whenever you guys are around!

111
00:08:08,580 --> 00:08:09,817
Could you guys be jinxed?

112
00:08:09,900 --> 00:08:13,017
I've heard about people who cause
disasters that endanger everyone?

113
00:08:13,100 --> 00:08:15,982
But if that's what you
are, I'd better stay away.

114
00:08:24,360 --> 00:08:27,654
I have just one bit of truth
for you, so listen closely.

115
00:08:28,980 --> 00:08:31,156
Whatever happens, we're on your side.

116
00:08:33,900 --> 00:08:34,730
Stay safe.

117
00:08:34,980 --> 00:08:37,509
Make sure you stay with
the others, got it?

118
00:08:44,900 --> 00:08:47,700
Let's go.

119
00:09:13,100 --> 00:09:15,453
Do you want me to open the cage for you?

120
00:09:15,540 --> 00:09:16,640
But I can't.

121
00:09:16,820 --> 00:09:18,697
I have no idea where the key is.

122
00:09:18,780 --> 00:09:20,545
And you're too big to let out.

123
00:09:22,160 --> 00:09:23,780
You're giving me an apple?

124
00:09:24,940 --> 00:09:26,705
But it doesn't make any sense.

125
00:09:26,800 --> 00:09:30,677
This apple's been cut with a knife, and
the color hasn't really changed yet.

126
00:09:30,760 --> 00:09:32,177
It looks totally fresh.

127
00:09:32,260 --> 00:09:34,020
Like it was cut a second ago.

128
00:09:35,360 --> 00:09:39,157
So, I guess there really must be
someone hiding somewhere on this boat.

129
00:09:39,240 --> 00:09:41,097
Where is the person who feeds you?

130
00:09:41,180 --> 00:09:43,017
Has he gone off and left you here?

131
00:09:43,100 --> 00:09:43,930
Huh?

132
00:09:47,960 --> 00:09:50,019
Whoa, you're a pretty smart monkey.

133
00:09:50,140 --> 00:09:51,728
Who trained you to do that?

134
00:10:02,840 --> 00:10:03,670
No way!

135
00:10:03,880 --> 00:10:06,704
A monkey like you is
actually into looking at...

136
00:10:07,440 --> 00:10:08,700
pin-ups of girls?

137
00:10:15,940 --> 00:10:19,937
Hey kid be careful there
they say an orangutan

138
00:10:20,020 --> 00:10:22,257
has five times the
strength of a normal human?

139
00:10:22,340 --> 00:10:25,697
So it could easily rip
off your arm come on

140
00:10:25,780 --> 00:10:27,897
stay with us in the
room on the other side!

141
00:10:27,980 --> 00:10:31,140
Don't go off by yourself oh okay.

142
00:10:44,440 --> 00:10:45,558
It's inconceivable.

143
00:10:45,920 --> 00:10:48,717
I've had Hierophant Green
search every inch of this ship,

144
00:10:48,800 --> 00:10:51,057
but I can't find a single
sign of human life aboard.

145
00:10:51,140 --> 00:10:55,258
We've searched every pipe and crevice,
but still came up empty-handed.

146
00:10:56,740 --> 00:10:57,570
Anything?

147
00:10:57,680 --> 00:10:58,720
It's no use.

148
00:10:58,880 --> 00:11:00,351
I can't get a connection.

149
00:11:00,520 --> 00:11:01,991
Well, try again, damn it.

150
00:11:07,060 --> 00:11:07,890
Gross.

151
00:11:07,973 --> 00:11:09,660
I feel sticky from the salt water.

152
00:11:17,820 --> 00:11:19,220
Huh?

153
00:11:43,100 --> 00:11:43,930
Let's go.

154
00:11:51,600 --> 00:11:52,430
Ah…

155
00:11:56,620 --> 00:11:58,020
Huh?

156
00:12:26,020 --> 00:12:28,840
Oh, my God.

157
00:12:56,680 --> 00:12:57,560
Hey!

158
00:13:01,100 --> 00:13:01,980
Jojo!

159
00:13:03,820 --> 00:13:06,320
Take your lock, you stinkin' ape!

160
00:13:09,260 --> 00:13:12,920
It seems that this ape isn't
your run-of-the-mill monkey.

161
00:13:13,360 --> 00:13:15,125
Could it be that he's the one?

162
00:13:25,880 --> 00:13:26,710
Wait.

163
00:13:26,820 --> 00:13:28,577
Who the hell ripped out that fan?

164
00:13:28,660 --> 00:13:29,490
Had to be him.

165
00:13:30,020 --> 00:13:32,857
So this ape's a stand user,
but where's the stand?

166
00:13:32,940 --> 00:13:35,317
I should be able to see the
damn thing, but I can't.

167
00:13:35,400 --> 00:13:36,929
It doesn't make any sense.

168
00:13:37,960 --> 00:13:38,790
What the?

169
00:13:38,920 --> 00:13:41,979
The steel propeller bent
on its own like it's alive!

170
00:13:43,460 --> 00:13:44,290
Jojo!

171
00:13:44,373 --> 00:13:46,400
Hey, what's going on here?

172
00:13:49,600 --> 00:13:50,740
Son of a bitch!

173
00:13:50,980 --> 00:13:53,657
There's no stand in sight
and somehow the window broke?

174
00:13:53,740 --> 00:13:54,880
Star Platinum!

175
00:14:10,220 --> 00:14:11,573
What's with this thing?

176
00:14:11,800 --> 00:14:14,624
The ape just sank into
the wall and disappeared.

177
00:14:15,260 --> 00:14:16,960
Hey, you saw that, right?

178
00:14:17,580 --> 00:14:18,580
Stay close to me.

179
00:14:18,880 --> 00:14:20,540
Something bad is going down.

180
00:14:21,360 --> 00:14:23,220
The ape vanished into the wall.

181
00:14:24,100 --> 00:14:27,060
But that orangutan has
to be the Stand user.

182
00:14:27,600 --> 00:14:31,137
When I touched it earlier, I felt
a Stand's energy coming from it.

183
00:14:31,220 --> 00:14:33,837
I have no doubt that he's
the one we're looking for.

184
00:14:33,920 --> 00:14:38,037
Doesn't make any sense why can't
I see this stand like I always do?

185
00:14:38,120 --> 00:14:43,017
Wait what If I'm seeing

186
00:14:43,100 --> 00:14:49,777
it already what's going

187
00:14:49,860 --> 00:14:54,877
on this isn't good it's
following us is the

188
00:14:54,960 --> 00:14:58,037
Freighter trying to is
it possible the ship

189
00:14:58,120 --> 00:15:02,160
itself is so the stand is
actually the freighter!

190
00:15:07,900 --> 00:15:09,420
Damn, you son of a...

191
00:15:10,180 --> 00:15:11,010
All of it!

192
00:15:11,460 --> 00:15:15,040
This ship itself and everything
on it is a gigantic stand!

193
00:15:15,360 --> 00:15:16,580
The entire ship?

194
00:15:16,800 --> 00:15:21,237
So there are stands that non-stand users
like that girl on the crew members can see?

195
00:15:21,320 --> 00:15:23,337
The only possible explanation for that is.

196
00:15:23,420 --> 00:15:25,277
That its immense energy
is making it possible.

197
00:15:25,360 --> 00:15:26,897
to be seen with the naked eye.

198
00:15:26,980 --> 00:15:30,880
But all this must demand a tremendous
amount of energy to operate.

199
00:15:31,100 --> 00:15:32,820
A stand as huge as this.

200
00:15:33,440 --> 00:15:36,080
Kick, send Hierophant green to Jotaro.

201
00:15:36,360 --> 00:15:37,937
He can help get us out of this.

202
00:15:38,020 --> 00:15:39,780
I can't do that.

203
00:15:39,940 --> 00:15:42,705
It's got a firm hold on
my stand and I'm stuck.

204
00:15:42,860 --> 00:15:44,677
This is what it means to face death.

205
00:15:44,760 --> 00:15:46,037
We fell for this trap.

206
00:15:46,120 --> 00:15:49,414
And now we're hopelessly
ensnared with no way to escape.

207
00:15:50,840 --> 00:15:52,820
The pressure keeps increasing.

208
00:15:53,400 --> 00:15:56,457
At this rate, our bodies
are going to be pulverized.

209
00:15:56,540 --> 00:15:57,937
We will be...

210
00:15:58,020 --> 00:15:59,660
Damn, we were careless.

211
00:16:00,000 --> 00:16:01,560
We've got to...

212
00:16:10,000 --> 00:16:13,900
The word that the orangutan
was pointing to was strength.

213
00:16:14,360 --> 00:16:17,720
It means force, energy, power, or aid.

214
00:16:17,920 --> 00:16:21,180
And it is the eighth
card of the tarot deck.

215
00:16:21,740 --> 00:16:26,420
It suggests challenge, a
strong will, and hidden powers.

216
00:16:41,860 --> 00:16:45,620
Damn ape, he thinks he's won already, huh?

217
00:16:46,400 --> 00:16:49,860
This entire ship is my
stand, and you've lost!

218
00:16:50,120 --> 00:16:54,560
You're totally outmatched and helpless,
and there's nothing you can do!

219
00:16:57,020 --> 00:16:59,060
Jotaro needed no explanation.

220
00:16:59,420 --> 00:17:01,773
He knew exactly what the ape was saying.

221
00:17:29,820 --> 00:17:30,917
Over here, monkey.

222
00:17:31,000 --> 00:17:33,176
That button's not part of your stand!

223
00:17:35,840 --> 00:17:36,817
Are you angry?

224
00:17:36,900 --> 00:17:41,194
I guess it wounded your pride, since
you thought you'd already beaten us.

225
00:17:41,800 --> 00:17:43,877
Oh, it's not hurt at all, is it?

226
00:17:43,960 --> 00:17:46,880
Because apes like you
don't have any pride.

227
00:17:50,140 --> 00:17:52,777
That's exactly what makes
you an ape and not a man.

228
00:17:52,860 --> 00:17:55,740
What's going to hurt now, is your head!

229
00:18:10,860 --> 00:18:11,720
Good grief.

230
00:18:18,840 --> 00:18:20,657
I've heard that, when frightened,

231
00:18:20,740 --> 00:18:24,617
animals show their stomachs to
signal their submission to the enemy.

232
00:18:24,700 --> 00:18:26,760
So you're asking me to forgive you?

233
00:18:29,260 --> 00:18:33,554
I'm afraid your actions have already
gone beyond the rules of the jungle.

234
00:18:35,040 --> 00:18:36,660
So I don't think so.

235
00:18:48,040 --> 00:18:48,880
What the?

236
00:18:49,040 --> 00:18:51,300
The pipes and walls are distorting!

237
00:18:51,460 --> 00:18:53,217
The whole ship is twisting up!

238
00:18:53,300 --> 00:18:55,540
Hey, be surprised about it later.

239
00:18:55,880 --> 00:18:57,520
This ship is about to sink.

240
00:18:58,040 --> 00:18:59,280
It's time to leave.

241
00:18:59,600 --> 00:19:01,129
Get back to the lifeboats!

242
00:19:07,680 --> 00:19:09,377
Wow, I can't believe it.

243
00:19:09,460 --> 00:19:11,197
The ship's shape is changing.

244
00:19:11,280 --> 00:19:13,574
It's turning into a shabby little boat.

245
00:19:14,340 --> 00:19:17,077
If I hadn't seen it myself,
I wouldn't believe it.

246
00:19:17,160 --> 00:19:19,984
That ape was traveling
the sea on his own stand.

247
00:19:20,460 --> 00:19:22,097
What terrifying power!

248
00:19:22,180 --> 00:19:25,057
That was the first time I've
encountered such energy.

249
00:19:25,140 --> 00:19:28,057
Hate to say it, but we were
completely overwhelmed this round.

250
00:19:28,140 --> 00:19:30,137
If Jotaro hadn't figured it out?

251
00:19:30,220 --> 00:19:32,000
we would have been done for.

252
00:19:32,520 --> 00:19:37,285
Are we going to encounter even more stands
with crazy unknown powers from now on?

253
00:19:37,420 --> 00:19:39,538
We'll have to be ready for anything.

254
00:19:40,780 --> 00:19:42,160
Hey, you want some gum?

255
00:19:43,080 --> 00:19:46,320
So we're going to be
drifting again. Good grief.

256
00:19:46,540 --> 00:19:47,777
My cigarettes are soaked.

257
00:19:47,860 --> 00:19:51,117
There'll be plenty of sun and
time for them to get dry, Jojo.

258
00:19:51,200 --> 00:19:55,082
We'll have to pray that we get
rescued and reach Singapore safely.

259
00:19:55,340 --> 00:19:56,300
And soon.

260
00:19:56,920 --> 00:19:59,297
It's been four days since we left Japan.

261
00:19:59,380 --> 00:20:03,980
There are 46 days until time
runs out for the Joestars.

262
00:20:13,680 --> 00:20:17,360
My lord, it would appear that
strength has been defeated.

263
00:20:17,820 --> 00:20:19,380
But have no fear.

264
00:20:19,740 --> 00:20:24,681
The remaining six stand users are all very
powerful and each deadlier than the last.

265
00:20:25,080 --> 00:20:26,757
And one of them is my son.

266
00:20:26,840 --> 00:20:29,320
His right arm shall crush our enemies.

267
00:20:29,840 --> 00:20:33,664
The Joestars will not pose a threat
when he's finished with them.

268
00:20:35,820 --> 00:20:37,860
You are a strange old woman.

269
00:20:38,180 --> 00:20:40,360
What is it that you desire the most?

270
00:20:40,720 --> 00:20:42,717
Oh, but I've told you many times.

271
00:20:42,800 --> 00:20:45,900
My only wish is to stay
by your side, my lord.

272
00:20:46,280 --> 00:20:49,140
Your guardian spirit
has unbelievable power.

273
00:20:49,500 --> 00:20:53,971
Your ability to escape trouble and your
strange life are the result of that.

274
00:20:54,700 --> 00:20:58,220
I would like to see your life unfold.

275
00:20:58,800 --> 00:21:01,040
It's the only thing I want.

276
00:21:04,140 --> 00:21:05,560
Once upon a time,

277
00:21:05,740 --> 00:21:10,457
there was a prince from the land of Sumatra
who traveled the seas seeking new lands.

278
00:21:10,540 --> 00:21:11,370
Eventually,

279
00:21:11,453 --> 00:21:14,797
he happened upon an island
inhabited by lions called Sinks,

280
00:21:14,880 --> 00:21:16,820
an island he named Singapore.

281
00:21:18,180 --> 00:21:22,037
Today, it's straits bustle with ships
and tankers from around the world.

282
00:21:22,120 --> 00:21:26,517
This nation that shares both Western and
Eastern heritage, thanks to free trade,

283
00:21:26,600 --> 00:21:27,894
is Tropical Singapore.

284
00:21:28,280 --> 00:21:30,840
Good grief, we finally
made it to dry land.

285
00:21:31,020 --> 00:21:33,237
We'll clean up and get
some rest at a hotel.

286
00:21:33,320 --> 00:21:36,377
Once we've recharged, we'll
figure out our route to Egypt.

287
00:21:36,460 --> 00:21:38,580
Alright, let's stay at that one.

288
00:22:12,240 --> 00:22:14,897
All the old paintings on the tomb.

289
00:22:14,980 --> 00:22:16,937
They do the sand dance, don't you know?

290
00:22:17,020 --> 00:22:19,177
If you move too quick, go away!

291
00:22:19,260 --> 00:22:21,557
They're falling down like a domino.

292
00:22:21,640 --> 00:22:24,257
All the buzzer men by the Nile.

293
00:22:24,340 --> 00:22:26,317
They got the money on a bed.

294
00:22:26,400 --> 00:22:27,917
Called crocodiles.

295
00:22:28,000 --> 00:22:30,877
I snapped their teeth on your cigarette.

296
00:22:30,960 --> 00:22:33,177
Falling tied to the hookah. I say.

297
00:22:33,260 --> 00:22:34,177
Walk

298
00:22:34,260 --> 00:22:41,260
like

299
00:22:41,400 --> 00:22:42,230
an Egyptian.

300
00:22:54,000 --> 00:22:56,897
The blonde waitresses take their trays.

301
00:22:56,980 --> 00:22:58,877
Spin around and they cross the floor.

302
00:22:58,960 --> 00:23:00,417
They've got the moves.

303
00:23:00,500 --> 00:23:03,557
You drop your drink then
they bring you more.

304
00:23:03,640 --> 00:23:06,197
All the school kids so sick of books.

305
00:23:06,280 --> 00:23:08,257
They're like the punk and the metal band.

306
00:23:08,340 --> 00:23:09,820
When the buzzer rings.

307
00:23:10,580 --> 00:23:12,497
They're walking like an Egyptian.

308
00:23:12,580 --> 00:23:15,157
All the kids in the marketplace say.

309
00:23:22,220 --> 00:23:24,040
walk like an Egyptian.

310
00:23:27,200 --> 00:23:31,435
Couldn't you guys at least give us a
chance to rest, persistent bastard?

311
00:23:31,520 --> 00:23:33,357
She'll be in danger if she stays with us.

312
00:23:33,440 --> 00:23:36,417
Polareff must have fallen
for Soul Sacrifice's trick.

313
00:23:36,500 --> 00:23:37,330
Train! Door!

314
00:23:37,800 --> 00:23:39,440
Who's among? Us all.

315
00:23:39,680 --> 00:23:41,240
Joestar, you bastard.
